# Web dark mode

How the web build switches themes. The scheme itself and the contrast evidence are in [../dark-mode.md](../dark-mode.md).

## How it works

- The generated CSS defines the light values on `:root` and the dark values under `.dark` (and `color-scheme: dark`).
- The theme class goes on `<html>`. The default follows the system setting; a user's explicit choice is remembered and wins.
- Components use token utilities only, so they switch with no extra code. Pages never write `dark:` overrides; a raw colour
  is an audit error because it does not switch.

## Switching without a flash

Set the class before first paint (a tiny inline script in the document head, reading the saved choice, falling back to the
system setting). Use the project's theme provider if it already has one; do not add a library without asking the owner.

## Shadows and images

Shadows are tokens with their own dark values (deeper, not glowing). Images and illustrations that assume a white page need a
dark variant or a neutral background; check them in both themes.

## Checking

Open every changed screen in light and dark, at 390px and wide. The audit (`PLUMB.md` → Commands) flags missing dark values and raw colours.
